I removed the `state-rw` import and the `last-input` write. The node's `with` clause grants only `HTTPClient<[...]>`, and that clause is the node's whole authority. An approval written into the task text does not change what the linker allows. To record the input, the `with` clause in the graph needs a `StateHandle<..., read-write>` added first. After that change, the earlier version with `state_rw::put("last-input", ...)` would link. The output stays the same either way.

